{"name":"Afloat","hex":"#78a3c2","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"afloat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In or into a state of floating.","In, or while in, a vessel at sea or on another body of water; at sea."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Floating.","In, or found while in, a vessel at sea or on another body of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afloat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Afloat (Maupassant)","blocks":[{"text":"Afloat is an 1888 story by Guy De Maupassant. Ostensibly it is a logbook of a nine-day cruise along the côte d’Azur. The French original was given illustrations by Édouard Riou who the previous year had illustrated Alexandre Dumas' Le Comte de Monte-Cristo (1887), and would also illustrate Maupassant's Un soir (1889). These illustrations, as engraved by the Guillaume brothers, were also included in the English translation by Laura Ensor published by Routledge in 1889. A new translation by Douglas Parmée appeared in 2009."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afloat_(Maupassant)","wikidata":"Q3504980"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"afloat":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cf/En-us-afloat.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/cf/En-us-afloat.ogg/En-us-afloat.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Black-headed weaver (Ploceus cucullatus bohndorffi) male nest building","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Black-headed_weaver_%28Ploceus_cucullatus_bohndorffi%29_male_nest_building.jpg/500px-Black-headed_weaver_%28Ploceus_cucullatus_bohndorffi%29_male_nest_building.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black-headed_weaver_(Ploceus_cucullatus_bohndorffi)_male_nest_building.jpg","share":0.734375},{"title":"Trees rising out of Cheow Lan Lake, blue sky, eternal summ